{
  "command": [
    "setup-claude.sh",
    "-p",
    "# Task: Fix login bug\n\n## Description\n\nThe login page returns a 500 error when the password is empty.\n\n## Ticket\n\nhttps://example.atlassian.net/browse/TICKET-100\n\n## Repository\n\nhttps://github.com/org/repo\n\n## Labels\n\nbug, backend\n\n## Instructions\n\n**IMPORTANT: You MUST open a merge request (MR/PR) before completing the task\nif you have created, modified, or deleted ANY files — including documentation,\nplans, configuration, and generated output. Never skip this step.**\n\n1. Configure git globally:\n   ```\n   git config --global user.name \"Osmia\"\n   git config --global user.email \"osmia@localhost\"\n   git config --global init.defaultBranch main\n   # Configure git credentials from SCM token env vars\n   if [ -n \"${GITLAB_TOKEN:-}\" ]; then\n     git config --global credential.helper store\n     echo \"https://oauth2:${GITLAB_TOKEN}@gitlab.com\" \u003e\u003e ~/.git-credentials\n   fi\n   if [ -n \"${GITHUB_TOKEN:-}\" ]; then\n     git config --global credential.helper store\n     echo \"https://x-access-token:${GITHUB_TOKEN}@github.com\" \u003e\u003e ~/.git-credentials\n   fi\n   ```\n\n2. Clone the repository to /workspace/repo:\n   ```\n   git clone --depth=1 https://github.com/org/repo /workspace/repo\n   ```\n\n3. Create a branch for your changes (use the same branch on every retry so work is not lost):\n   ```\n   git checkout -b osmia/TICKET-100\n   ```\n\n4. Commit and push your changes to that branch at logical checkpoints:\n   ```\n   git add -A \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"wip: \u003cshort description\u003e\"\n   git push origin osmia/TICKET-100\n   ```\n\n5. Open a merge request. This step is MANDATORY — do not skip it.\n   Use `glab` (for GitLab) or `gh` (for GitHub).\n   Write a clear, well-structured MR description covering: what changed, why, and how to verify.\n   The MR title MUST end with ` [osmia/TICKET-100]` so the ticket is traceable from the MR.\n   Include `References: https://example.atlassian.net/browse/TICKET-100` in the MR description body.\n   Example for GitLab:\n   ```\n   cd /workspace/repo\n   glab auth login --hostname gitlab.com --token \"$GITLAB_TOKEN\"\n   glab mr create --fill --title \"\u003cconcise title\u003e [osmia/TICKET-100]\" --description \"\u003cfull description\u003e\"\n   ```\n\n6. When the full task is complete, write /workspace/result.json containing:\n   `{\"success\": true, \"summary\": \"\u003cone-line summary\u003e\", \"branch_name\": \"osmia/TICKET-100\", \"merge_request_url\": \"\u003cMR URL from step 5\u003e\"}`\n",
    "--output-format",
    "stream-json",
    "--max-turns",
    "50",
    "--dangerously-skip-permissions",
    "--verbose",
    "--mcp-config",
    "/workspace/.mcp.json",
    "--json-schema",
    "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"success\": {\"type\": \"boolean\"},\n    \"summary\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n    \"merge_request_url\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n    \"branch_name\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n    \"tests_passed\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n    \"tests_failed\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n    \"tests_added\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"success\", \"summary\"]\n}"
  ],
  "env": {
    "CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC": "1",
    "OSMIA_REPO_URL": "https://github.com/org/repo",
    "OSMIA_TASK_ID": "task-fresh-1",
    "OSMIA_TICKET_ID": "TICKET-100"
  },
  "secret_key_refs": {
    "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY": {
      "secret_name": "osmia-anthropic-key",
      "key": "api_key"
    }
  },
  "volumes": [
    {
      "name": "workspace",
      "mount_path": "/workspace"
    },
    {
      "name": "config",
      "mount_path": "/config",
      "read_only": true
    },
    {
      "name": "home",
      "mount_path": "/home/osmia"
    },
    {
      "name": "tmp",
      "mount_path": "/tmp"
    }
  ]
}
